WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:05.020
Some of the biggest stars in the world sign
up for the shows set in the "Yellowstone" universe.

00:00:05.098 --> 00:00:09.300
But the Dutton clan saga can also make stars
out of young actors, including the familiar

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:12.090
face who plays Spencer in "1923."

00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:15.820
"Yellowstone" has proven to be the franchise
that can't be stopped.

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:20.770
The show just finished its fifth season and
it's continuing to rack up impressive viewership numbers.

00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:25.210
Plus, a slew of spinoffs are keeping the legend
of the Dutton family alive and well.

00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:29.890
First, there was "1883," which tracked the
family's migration from Texas to Montana.

00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:34.800
By the time of "1923," the Duttons are secure
in their Montana property, but there are various

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:36.260
hardships looming.

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:41.640
"1923" features several incredible stars,
including Harrison Ford, who plays Jacob Dutton,

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:43.820
and Helen Mirren, who plays Cara Dutton.

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:48.361
Jacob and Cara's nephew Spencer Dutton, a
World War I veteran who now spends much of

00:00:48.361 --> 00:00:52.577
his time tracking big game across Africa,
is quickly becoming a fan favorite.

00:00:52.577 --> 00:00:54.257
"My goodness."

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:59.050
The actor who plays him, Brandon Sklenar,
may not be a household name like Ford and

00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:02.410
Mirren just yet, but he has ample credits
to his name.

00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:05.080
Sklenar has mostly appeared in supporting
roles so far.

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:09.500
According to IMDb, he got his start in several
projects, including "Truth Be Told," "Fall

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:10.700
Into Me," and "New Girl."

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:16.009
He finally got a chance to show his range
with a major part in the 2018 film "Mapplethorpe."

00:01:16.009 --> 00:01:20.880
The movie follows the life of famed photographer
Robert Mapplethorpe, played by Matt Smith.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:24.909
Partway through the film, Robert hires his
younger brother Edward, played by Sklenar,

00:01:24.909 --> 00:01:26.270
to work as his assistant.

00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:29.840
While the two seem to get along at first,
it's clear there's tension between them.

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:33.909
Their dynamic leads to one of the best scenes
in the movie, where the two have a blow-out

00:01:33.909 --> 00:01:36.530
fight, and it's here that Sklenar gets to
shine.

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:38.186
"I have this much!

00:01:38.186 --> 00:01:39.186
This much!

00:01:40.884 --> 00:01:42.189
I need to start my own life."

00:01:42.189 --> 00:01:46.390
In an interview about the film with The Upcoming
at the Tribeca Film Festival, he said,

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:01.410
Sklenar also popped in for two episodes of
HBO's "Westworld."

00:02:01.410 --> 00:02:06.964
He played Henry, who, in Season 4, went on
an extremely bad date with Evan Rachel Wood's Christina.

00:02:06.964 --> 00:02:11.600
The show's final season sees Christina working
as a video game writer for Olympiad Entertainment.

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:15.050
When she goes on her date with Henry, he's
pretty much full of himself and can't even

00:02:15.050 --> 00:02:18.200
be bothered to remember what it is Christina
does for a living.

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:22.574
That doesn't stop him from hitting on her,
prompting her to leave in the middle of their dinner.

00:02:22.574 --> 00:02:26.920
Despite the small role, a sampling of Redditors
found the character compelling, particularly

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:29.480
when he hummed as Christina walked away.

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:32.379
Several wondered whether Henry was a fly-controlled
human.

00:02:32.379 --> 00:02:36.580
Regardless of what you think, it's that attention
to detail that made the show such a hit.

00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:38.292
One Redditor summed it up well, writing,

00:02:43.529 --> 00:02:48.550
Before stepping into the world of "1923,"
Sklenar could last be seen playing Burt Reynolds

00:02:48.550 --> 00:02:49.599
in "The Offer."

00:02:49.599 --> 00:02:54.190
The limited series told the story of the making
of "The Godfather," and in the final episode,

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:58.360
Film producer Al Ruddy, played by Miles Teller,
brings a treatment to Reynolds for what would

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:00.430
eventually become "The Longest Yard."

00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:03.470
Of course, Ruddy finds himself between a rock
and a hard place.

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:07.069
The studio wants to capitalize on the success
of "The Godfather" with a sequel, but the

00:03:07.069 --> 00:03:09.019
producer is ready to move on.

00:03:09.019 --> 00:03:12.709
Throughout the remainder of the episode, Reynolds
grows impatient with Ruddy because he has

00:03:12.709 --> 00:03:16.150
other projects on the line, but eventually,
they find a way to work it out.

00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:21.845
After mostly supporting roles, with "1923,"
Sklernar really gets to step out front and center.

00:03:21.845 --> 00:03:24.630
Here's hoping it's the first of many star
turns for the actor.

